---
layout: base
title: "A Living World"
description: "The living lore encyclopedia for Ahvantir — the great city of Aru'Mas and the world beyond."
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero__inner">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">The Lore Encyclopedia of</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">Ahvantir</h1>
    <p class="hero__subtitle">A world shaped by ancient pacts, layered histories,<br>and the city that never sleeps — <em>Aru'Mas</em>.</p>
    {# Three actions used to mean three button styles -- gold, teal, outline --
       side by side, which reads as three equally important things rather than
       one primary and two alternatives. Entering the world is the primary;
       the other two are the same weight as each other. #}
    <div class="hero__actions">
      <a href="/play/" class="btn btn--play"><span class="btn--play__sigil" aria-hidden="true">⚜</span> Enter the world</a>
      <a href="/articles/" class="btn btn--onDark">Browse articles</a>
      <a href="/search/" class="btn btn--onDark">Search the records</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-intro">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="home-intro__text">
      <p>
        These records belong to the Aru'Mas Historical Society — compiled from guild archives,
        temple manuscripts, noble house memoirs, and accounts recovered from the ruins of older ages.
        What follows is not a complete history. It is what survived.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ahvantir is a world of deliberate complexity: heroic founders who committed atrocities,
        gods who may be tyrants, and a city where every district keeps its own secrets.
        Read carefully. Not all sources agree.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cryptex-section">
  <div class="container cryptex-container">
    <h2 class="cryptex-heading">The Cryptex</h2>
    <p class="cryptex-subheading">Align three runes. Consult the stone. Each sequence unlocks an article hidden within the archives.</p>

    <div class="cryptex-wheel" aria-label="Rune selector">
      {% for pos in [0, 1, 2] %}
      <div class="cryptex-stone" data-pos="{{ pos }}" role="group" aria-label="Rune position {{ pos + 1 }}">
        <button class="cryptex-btn-up" data-pos="{{ pos }}" type="button" aria-label="Previous rune">▲</button>
        <div class="cryptex-rune-face">
          <span class="cryptex-rune" aria-hidden="true">ᚠ</span>
          <span class="cryptex-rune-name">Fehu</span>
        </div>
        <button class="cryptex-btn-down" data-pos="{{ pos }}" type="button" aria-label="Next rune">▼</button>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <button id="cryptex-consult" class="btn btn--primary cryptex-consult-btn" type="button">
      Consult the Cryptex
    </button>

    <div id="cryptex-result" class="cryptex-result" aria-live="polite"></div>

    <div class="cryptex-discoveries" id="cryptex-discoveries">
      {# aria-expanded says the control is collapsible; aria-controls says what
         it collapses. Without the pair a screen reader announces the state of
         something it cannot point the user at. #}
      <button class="discoveries-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="discoveries-list" title="Rune sequences you have unlocked">Your discoveries (0)</button>
      <ul class="discoveries-list" id="discoveries-list" role="list"></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="application/json" id="cryptex-data">[{% for article in collections.allArticles %}{% if not loop.first %},{% endif %}{"title":{{ article.data.title | jsonscript | safe }},"url":"{{ article.url }}"}{% endfor %}]</script>
<script src="/assets/js/cryptex.js"></script>

<section class="home-categories">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Browse by subject</h2>
    <div class="category-grid">
      {% for cat in meta.categories %}
      <a href="/articles/#{{ cat.slug }}" class="category-card" style="--cat-color: {{ cat.color }}">
        <span class="category-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
               stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">{{ cat.icon | safe }}</svg>
        </span>
        <h3 class="category-card__title">{{ cat.label }}</h3>
        <p class="category-card__desc">{{ cat.description }}</p>
      </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% if collections.allArticles.length %}
<section class="home-recent">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 class="section-title">Recently added</h2>
      <a href="/recently-added/" class="section-head__more">See what changed</a>
    </div>
    <div class="article-grid">
      {% set recentArticles = collections.allArticles | reverse %}
      {% for article in recentArticles %}
      {% if loop.index <= 6 %}
      <a href="{{ article.url }}" class="article-card">
        {% if article.data.category %}
        <span class="article-card__cat">{{ article.data.category | capitalize }}</span>
        {% endif %}
        <h3 class="article-card__title">{{ article.data.title }}</h3>
        {% if article.data.description %}
        <p class="article-card__desc">{{ article.data.description | stripWikilinks }}</p>
        {% endif %}
      </a>
      {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="home-recent__more">
      <a href="/articles/" class="btn btn--ghost">View all {{ collections.allArticles.length }} articles</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% else %}
<section class="home-recent">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Recently added</h2>
    <p class="home-empty">No articles yet. Add markdown files to <code>src/articles/</code> to see them here.</p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}
